## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta (C1).** A path beyond the four, a product byte, a workflow, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `verify-suite.sh` or the counts file changed = **Blocker**; a removed line beyond the seven, or a lost/added/renamed cell, `.only/.skip/.todo`, a retry, a suppression comment = **Major**; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card id in an added line or any message = **Blocker**; a brief or work number token in an added line = **Minor**; non-ASCII in the added lines = **Major**; a head other than `a4d7ecaa` = STOP; four commits = **Note** (a merge commit of the gated head keeps them: C-190, C-68).
- **G-2 the cells still prove what they proved (C4, C5, C8; class "a re-shaped test site").** A re-shaped cell green under its guard mutant (MU4 at the head, the emergency-name mutant for the erasure cell, MB1) = **Major**; the plant multiset differing base to head = **Major**; a cell title or id changed, or a per-file `Tests:` differing without a reason = **Major**; a cell red at the head on the unbroken product = **Major**; a cell red at both ends = reported, graded by its cause.
- **G-3 the helper and the script (C6, C7).** Different bytes or a different error code for the same input in the helper = **Major**; a short write on a large body (L4) = **Major**; a descriptor left open on a failing path = **Major**; the tamper control reading 0 errors in a head run = **Major**; a real record written with different bytes or a different name = **Major**; the cap changing a real record = **Blocker**; the cap cutting only an artificial over-cap record = **Note**.
- **G-4 CodeQL and CI (C3, C9).** **An open alert on the PR ref at a line the PR added = Blocker for the landing** (the `CodeQL` check fails and the ruleset's thresholds block the merge; record each alert, its main twin and its severity; the PR cannot land at this head); an open alert on a line the PR did not add = reported, not this PR's; a failing check-run on the head other than `CodeQL` = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, conditional; the verify pair differing from the committed counts file in either direction = **Blocker**; a whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**. **Always Note:** the author field, a dependabot vulnerabilities line, main's #111 and #274/#116/#97/#234/#238 still open on main (C-209: closure is read after a merge, never on a PR), the stale PR-body sentence about pending checks, the Linux runner and node 24 if the hosted `build` is not complete, the builder's local node v26.
- **G-5 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker or Major = `NO GO round 1 of 2`: FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list (the sites and cells you proved, with the cells that prove them), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the alert numbers, and the fix shape in prose (one new commit on the same branch, forward only, no rebase; a new head is a new gate round 2 of 2 and a new CodeQL run). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`. Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional. `model-routing.md:111` (G-cap): "Two NO GO rounds on one class: STOP. Ship the closed instances, ticket the residue with the tester's cells attached. A third round needs [the product owner]'s word on a card." The landing is a merge commit, so the four commit messages, not the PR title, become history: say which text lands.

